<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ptolemaeus of Commagene</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ptolemaeus was the founder of the kingdom of Commagene in south-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anatolia">Anatolia</a>. A Seleucid governor of the region, he broke away from the weakening <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seleucid-empire">Seleucid Empire</a> around 163 BCE and ruled as an independent king until about 130 BCE. His descendants, among them <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mithridates-i-callinicus">Mithridates I Callinicus</a> and Antiochus I Theos, ruled Commagene until it came under Roman control.</p></div>
